    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean yeah i get that, but i literally just looked it up and people say peroxide is actually great for cleaning deep wounds because it bubbles out the dirt. if i just use a lot of that and maybe some neosporin, and keep it covered, wouldn't that take care of the bacteria? i'm just really trying to avoid a huge medical bill for something that seems pretty minor. surely i can just monitor it for a few days and if it looks red i'll go in then?",
